# A do-while loop whose latch is false at its first evaluation runs
# once (ptxas, and on an RTX 4090): with no guard before it, its count
# is max(T, 1) per entry, as LLVM's ScalarEvolution counts a rotated
# loop's backedges from max(RHS, Start), so 1 where the latch solves to
# 5 - 10 = -5. With the parameter unbound the second loop reads
# `max(param_1 - 10, 1)`. The RTX 4090 record at n = 5 agrees on both
# stores' L2 sectors.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/latch_exits_first.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=FREE "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/latch_exits_first.ptx --bind 1:n=5 | FileCheck "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/latch_exits_first.ptx --ncu %fixtures/micro/latch_exits_first.ncu.json | FileCheck --check-prefix=REC "%s"
CHECK-LABEL: kernel micro_latch_exits_first
CHECK: trips = 1
CHECK: totals [static]:
CHECK: global bytes: load 0 B, store 8 B
CHECK-LABEL: kernel micro_latch_exits_first_param
CHECK: trips = 1
CHECK: totals [static]:
CHECK: global bytes: load 0 B, store 8 B
FREE-LABEL: kernel micro_latch_exits_first_param
FREE: trips = max(param_1 - 10, 1)
REC-LABEL: kernel micro_latch_exits_first_param
REC: trips = 1
REC: measured L2 sectors of global accesses: 2 lines agree (2 exact, 0 within a range, 0 within a bound), 0 differ
